{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sqrt_add_inv_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sqrt_add_inv_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L309-L314","doc":"**AM-GM for `√x + 1/√x`**: for `x > 0`, `√x + 1/√x ≥ 2`.\n\nDirect corollary of `add_inv_ge_two` applied to `t := √x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.add_inv_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.add_inv_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L290-L307","doc":"**AM-GM for `t + 1/t`**: for `t > 0`, `t + 1/t ≥ 2`.\n\nProof: `(t - 1)² ≥ 0` expands to `t² - 2t + 1 ≥ 0`, dividing\nby `t` gives `t - 2 + 1/t ≥ 0`, i.e. `t + 1/t ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Real.sqrt_lt_of_lt_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Real.sqrt_lt_of_lt_sq","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L280-L288","doc":"**Bracketing helper**: if `0 ≤ x` and `x < a^2`, then\n`Real.sqrt x < a` (assuming `0 ≤ a`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Real.lt_sqrt_of_sq_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Real.lt_sqrt_of_sq_lt","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L270-L278","doc":"**Bracketing helper**: if `a > 0` and `a^2 < x`, then\n`a < Real.sqrt x`. Lifted from `Real.sqrt_lt_sqrt` with the\n`Real.sqrt_sq` simplification baked in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sqrt_mul_half_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sqrt_mul_half_denom","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L254-L268","doc":"For `x > 0`, the function `t ↦ t + 1/t` evaluated at\n`t = Real.sqrt x` is non-negative and admits a clean\ncross-multiplication identity:\n`(Real.sqrt x) · ((Real.sqrt x) + 1 / (Real.sqrt x))\n   = x + 1`,\ni.e. multiplying the QOU half-denominator by `sqrt x` clears\nthe inverse, yielding a closed-form polynomial in `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.q_half_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.q_half_denom","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L248-L252","doc":"The QOU \"denominator\" `q^(1/2) + q^(-1/2)` equals\n`sqrt q + 1 / sqrt q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Real.rpow_neg_half_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Real.rpow_neg_half_eq","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L243-L246","doc":"For `x > 0`, `x^(-(1/2) : ℝ) = 1 / Real.sqrt x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.Real.rpow_half_eq_sqrt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.Real.rpow_half_eq_sqrt","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L230-L241","doc":"`x^(1/2 : ℝ) = Real.sqrt x` (for any real `x`; both sides\nare zero on the negative reals via the rpow / sqrt\nconventions).  Symmetric form of Mathlib's\n`Real.sqrt_eq_rpow`.\n\nUpstream status: this is the `.symm` of Mathlib's `Real.sqrt_eq_rpow`\n(present in the pinned v4.24).  A named `Real.rpow_one_div_two` is\n**not** in the pinned Mathlib (probed 2026-06-26 — `unknown constant`),\nso this local convenience wrapper stays until/unless one lands upstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sum_eq_finsetSum_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sum_eq_finsetSum_getD","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L204-L219","doc":"A natural-number list's sum equals the indexed Finset sum\nof its `getD ·  0` accessor. Mechanical induction on the list.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List` —\nstandard sum-is-finset-sum identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_map_reverse_eq_of_forall_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_map_reverse_eq_of_forall_commute","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L196-L202","doc":"Mapped form: when a family `f` commutes with itself globally, the\nproduct over `xs.map f` is reversal-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_reverse_eq_of_pairwise_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_reverse_eq_of_pairwise_commute","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L179-L194","doc":"**Reversing a list does not change its product when the list's own\nelements commute pairwise** — the non-commutative-monoid form of\n`prod_reverse_eq`.\n\nNote this needs nothing new from Mathlib: `List.Perm.prod_eq'`\n(`Mathlib/Algebra/BigOperators/Group/List/Lemmas.lean:56`) already\ntakes exactly a `Pairwise Commute` hypothesis, and `List.reverse_perm`\nsupplies the permutation.  Recorded here because the QOU call site had\nbeen looking for a `foldl`/`foldr` bridge lemma instead, which is a\ndifferent (and, for that call site, unnecessary) statement — see the\ncorrection on `§3a` below and on\n`QOU.TMCorrespondence.MatrixChainEqBuildChains`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.pairwise_of_forall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.pairwise_of_forall","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L172-L177","doc":"A `Pairwise` relation that holds for *every* pair holds along any list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_reverse_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_reverse_eq","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L158-L161","doc":"`xs.reverse.prod = xs.prod` in a `CommMonoid`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_eq_of_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_eq_of_perm","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L144-L150","doc":"Permutation-invariance of products in a commutative monoid\n(specialisation of `List.Perm.prod_eq` for use as a lookup\ntarget by automation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.foldl_eq_foldr_of_commute_init","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.foldl_eq_foldr_of_commute_init","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L112-L142","doc":"**Foldl/foldr equality from a Commute hypothesis on the\ninitial accumulator**: foldl and foldr produce the same\nresult over an arbitrary `Monoid` whenever the initial\naccumulator commutes with every list element.\n\nNote: pairwise commutativity *among* the list elements is not\nneeded for this form — the result is `init * xs.prod` either\nway (foldl) or `xs.prod * init` (foldr), and these are equal\niff `init` commutes with `xs.prod`, which is exactly the\n`Commute init x for all x` hypothesis (via `commute_init_prod`).\n\n**CORRECTION 2026-09-05: this does NOT discharge\n`MatrixChainEqBuildChains`.**  The sentence removed here claimed it did\n\"after some rearrangement\".  It does not, and the reason is structural\nrather than a missing rearrangement: this lemma moves the *initial\naccumulator* from one end of the product to the other and leaves the\nlist order alone (both sides are `init * xs.prod` / `xs.prod * init`).\n`matrixChain` does not have an accumulator problem — it **reverses the\nlist** (`matrixChain (x :: l) = matrixChain l * f x`, so\n`matrixChain seq = (seq.map f).reverse.prod`).  The lemma that applies\nis `prod_reverse_eq_of_pairwise_commute` in §3b.  (That call site is now\nfully closed — `QOU.TMCorrespondence.matrixChain_eq_buildChains` is proved\nunconditionally as of 2026-09-05, and the class has an instance.)\n\nThe lemma itself is correct and is kept; only its claimed consequence\nwas wrong. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.List.commute_init_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.List.commute_init_prod","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L100-L110","doc":"`Commute init xs.prod` follows from `init` commuting with\nevery element of `xs`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.foldl_eq_foldr_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.foldl_eq_foldr_comm","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L85-L90","doc":"For a *commutative* monoid, foldl and foldr agree: both\nproduce `init * xs.prod = xs.prod * init`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.foldl_mul_eq_prod_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.foldl_mul_eq_prod_mul","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L76-L81","doc":"Backward-compatible alias matching the original CommMonoid\nname (the statement and proof generalise to any Monoid). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.List.foldr_mul_eq_prod_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.List.foldr_mul_eq_prod_mul","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L66-L74","doc":"Companion for `foldr`: `List.foldr (· * ·) init xs = xs.prod * init`.\nAlso `Monoid`-level — no commutativity required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.List.foldl_mul_eq_mul_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.List.foldl_mul_eq_mul_prod","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L51-L64","doc":"For *any* monoid, `List.foldl (· * ·) init xs` equals\n`init * xs.prod`. Holds for arbitrary `Monoid` — no\ncommutativity needed; the proof uses associativity only.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List` —\nMathlib has `List.foldl_assoc` for `init = 1`; this is the\n`init ≠ 1` generalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prod_insertionSort_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prod_insertionSort_eq","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L40-L47","doc":"Sorting (by any relation) preserves the list's product\n(for commutative monoids).\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Data.List.Sort`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sum_insertionSort_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sum_insertionSort_eq","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt.lean#L28-L38","doc":"Sorting (by any relation) preserves the list's sum.\n\nProof: `insertionSort` is a permutation; `List.Perm.sum_eq`\ntransfers sum across permutations.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Data.List.Sort` or\n`Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}